silm:instances_papers_18_presheaf_semantics_03_olog_node_arrow_law_concrete_anchor_7_commute_eq#mittensvetrecordpresheafanchornode7 silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensVetRecordPresheafAnchorNode7 is the commuting equation P(g.f) = P(f).P(g), concretely the assertion that ownership-then-mass-lookup equals composite-lookup on Mittens records. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'commute_eq', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
